  "ref": "ACT.2.33",
  "review_notes": [
    "Corrected tei dexiai under rule 102: the article now takes the discontinuous *by the ... hand* headed on *hand* and the substantival adjective a bare *right*, matching ACT.2.11's ta megaleia -> *the ... works*. The previous reading gave *by the* to the article and *right hand* to the adjective under rule 17's generic-noun clause, which rule 102 scopes to anarthrous Greek.",
    "The anarthrous ek dexion mou at ACT.2.25 and ACT.2.34 is deliberately left as it stands: no article competes there, so rule 17's generic-noun clause governs and *hand* remains the adjective's supplied completion headed on *right*. Reading *right hand* as the lexeme's own English gloss rather than an adjective plus a supplied noun would leave all three verses alone, and that reading remains defensible; this chapter takes *hand* as supplied, as the notes at 2.25, 2.33 and 2.34 already did, and rule 102 then decides the arthrous case.",
    "No status changes, so the BSB comparison for this verse is unaffected."
  ]
